This TypeScript loop never prints anything, although Claude clearly answers. What is wrong?

```ts
for await (const message of query({ prompt: "Summarize this project" })) {
  if (message.type === "assistant") {
    for (const block of message.content ?? []) {
      if (block.type === "text") console.log(block.text);
    }
  }
}
```

This TypeScript code fails to compile with `Property 'result' does not exist on type 'SDKResultMessage'`. What is the right fix?

```ts
for await (const message of query({ prompt })) {
  if (message.type === "result") {
    console.log(message.result);
  }
}
```
